cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SHEPHARD in your work, please cite the paper below."
title: SHEPHARD
abstract: >-
  SHEPHARD (Sequence-based Hierarchical and Extendable Platform for
  High-throughput Analysis of Regions of Disorder) is a Python framework for
  reading, annotating, and analyzing large protein datasets, enabling
  reproducible integrative analysis of complex sequence annotations at
  proteome-wide scales.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/holehouse-lab/shephard"
url: "https://shephard.readthedocs.io/"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - proteome
  - protein
  - intrinsically disordered regions
  - sequence annotation
